{
  "category": "Mouse Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "Its long tail serves as a ground to protect itself from its own high voltage power.",
      "version": "red"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its long tail serves as a ground to protect itself from its own high voltage power.",
      "version": "blue"
    },
    {
      "text": "When electricity builds up inside its body, it becomes feisty. It also glows in the dark.",
      "version": "yellow"
    },
    {
      "text": "When its electricity builds, its muscles are stimu lated, and it becomes more aggressive than usual.",
      "version": "gold"
    },
    {
      "text": "If the electric pouches in its cheeks become fully charged, both ears will stand straight up.",
      "version": "silver"
    },
    {
      "text": "If its electric pouches run empty, it raises its tail to gather electricity from the atmosphere.",
      "version": "crystal"
    },
    {
      "text": "If the electrical sacks become excessively charged, RAICHU plants its tail in the ground and discharges. Scorched patches of ground will be found near this POKéMON’s nest.",
      "version": "ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "This POKéMON exudes a weak electrical charge from all over its body that makes it take on a slight glow in darkness. RAICHU searches for electricity by planting its tail in the ground.",
      "version": "sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "If it stores too much electricity, its behavior turns aggressive. To avoid this, it occasionally discharges excess energy and calms itself down.",
      "version": "emerald"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its electric charges can reach even 100,000 volts. Careless contact can cause even an Indian elephant to faint.",
      "version": "firered"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its long tail serves as a ground to protect itself from its own high-voltage power.",
      "version": "leafgreen"
    },
    {
      "text": "It turns aggressive if it has too much electricity in its body. It discharges power through its tail.",
      "version": "diamond"
    },
    {
      "text": "It can loose 100,000-volt bursts of electricity, instantly downing foes several times its size.",
      "version": "pearl"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its tail discharges electricity into the ground, protecting it from getting shocked.",
      "version": "platinum"
    },
    {
      "text": "When its electricity builds, its muscles are stimulated, and it becomes more aggressive than usual.",
      "version": "heartgold"
    },
    {
      "text": "If the electric pouches in its cheeks become fully charged, both ears will stand straight up.",
      "version": "soulsilver"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its tail discharges electricity into the ground, protecting it from getting shocked.",
      "version": "black"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its tail discharges electricity into the ground, protecting it from getting shocked.",
      "version": "white"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its tail discharges electricity into the ground, protecting it from getting shocked.",
      "version": "black-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its tail discharges electricity into the ground, protecting it from getting shocked.",
      "version": "white-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "When its electricity builds, its muscles are stimulated, and it becomes more aggressive than usual.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "It can loose 100,000-volt bursts of electricity, instantly downing foes several times its size.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "If the electrical sacs become excessively charged, Raichu plants its tail in the ground and discharges. Scorched patches of ground will be found near this Pokémon’s nest.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "This Pokémon exudes a weak electrical charge from all over its body that makes it take on a slight glow in darkness. Raichu plants its tail in the ground to discharge electricity.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "It unleashes electric shocks that can reach 100,000 volts. When agitated, it can knock out even an Indian elephant.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "It becomes aggressive when it has electricity stored up. At such times, even its Trainer has to take care to avoid being attacked.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "As electricity builds up inside its body, it becomes more aggressive. One theory is that the electricity buildup is actually causing stress.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "Because so many Trainers like the way Pikachu looks, you don’t see this Pokémon very often.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "When electricity builds up inside its body, it becomes feisty. It also glows in the dark.",
      "version": "lets-go-pikachu"
    },
    {
      "text": "When electricity builds up inside its body, it becomes feisty. It also glows in the dark.",
      "version": "lets-go-eevee"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its long tail serves as a ground to protect itself from its own high-voltage power.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "If its electric pouches run empty, it raises its tail to gather electricity from the atmosphere.",
      "version": "shield"
    },
    {
      "text": "It can discharge bursts of electricity exceeding 100,000 volts— a single strike with that amount of power would incapacitate one of the Copperajah of my homeland.",
      "version": "legends-arceus"
    }
  ],
